t types: auto      Schemas for custom document types: manual          See Setup Types.\nAction:", "\nTitle: Prefilled Setup Types for Schema Fields\nDescription: When you add data fields to schemas, the service now prefills the Setup Type field with default values.   Depending on whether you use the service plan premium edition or base edition, the default values are as follows:    Premium edition:      Schemas for standard and custom document types: auto          Base edition:      Schemas for standard document types: auto      Schemas for custom document types: manual          See Setup Types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-11\nValid as Of: 2023-12-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3769 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Document AI Basic UI\nDescription: There have been several security improvements on the SAP Document AI basic UI.  See Using the SAP Document AI Basic UI (Base Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-11\nValid as Of: 2023-12-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3770 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for X.509 Authentication\nDescription: The SAP Document AI APIs now support X.509 authentication.  See Enable X.509 Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-11\nValid as Of: 2023-12-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2751 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process Visibility - Authorization\nDescription: You can define granular access by configuring data-level authorization to filter scenario instances based on the logged-in user. This enables users to view and track instances that are specific to their responsibilities.   See Track Instances 